WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:11.088
Ahead of wedding-parent makeup, be especially careful with cosmetic surgery or intensive skin procedures.

2
00:00:11.424 --> 00:00:21.360
Eye or lower blepharoplasty surgery should ideally be done at least six months before the wedding, factoring in the risk of side effects and the time needed for the look to settle naturally.

3
00:00:21.696 --> 00:00:28.584
Botox around the eyes should also be finished at least two to three months ahead so your expression doesn't look stiff on the day.

4
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:33.936
In particular, avoid laser treatments for melasma removal in spring or summer,

5
00:00:34.272 --> 00:00:46.416
because if the skin, left vulnerable after the procedure, doesn't get thorough sun protection and moisturizing, pigmentation can worsen and leave the face looking blotchy.

6
00:00:46.752 --> 00:00:50.448
"I guess laser treatments just don't agree with me," people end up saying.

7
00:00:50.784 --> 00:01:01.728
Also, using a rich functional cosmetic you don't normally use right before the wedding can trigger sudden breakouts or allergic reactions that get in the way of the makeup,

8
00:01:02.064 --> 00:01:07.896
so patch-test any new product first and only use it once you're sure it causes no reaction.
